    <field name="scopecontent_teim">Cabinet card portrait of Catherine &#34;Katie&#34; King by Bloomingdale Bros., 59th St. &amp; 3rd Ave., N.Y. Identified (verso) as &#34;Aunt Katie King (Uncle Henry[&#39;s] Katie) / Died on the Scolum [sic] / June 15, 1904 / Were going to be married / Sept 15, 1904.&#34;</field>
    <field name="scopecontent_teim">A notation (verso) by N-YHS staff reads: &#34;b. 1888 [sic] in Ireland lived 311 E 37th St / fiancée of Henry Liebenow.&#34; Henry Liebenow died in 1900, so Katie King was more likely engaged to marry Henry Wulf (1876-1912), brother of Anna (Wulf) Liebenow. According to her death certificate, Catherine King was 26 when she died on June 15, 1904. That places her birth circa 1878.</field>
